{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-68176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{4x}-\\frac{1}{x+5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-68176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4x}-\\frac{1}{x+5} & =\\frac{x+5-4x}{4x(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-3x}{4x(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n4x(x+5)=0\\,⟹\\,x=0\\,,\\,x=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=0$ and $x=-5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-68176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3bf15859013a041badc2d3845fd1acf72b0f97b9d8b99f85c723c09cbdf69333"} {"question" "q-68176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-68176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-5"] ["math" "x=5"] ["text" "$x=0$ and $x=-5$"] ["text" "$x=0$ and $x=5$"] ["text" "No vertical asymptotes"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-68176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=0$ and $x=-5$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-107070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{(x-5)({x}^{3}+1)}{{x}^{2}-4x-5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-107070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-5)({x}^{3}+1)}{{x}^{2}-4x-5} & =\\frac{(x-5)(x+1)({x}^{2}-x+1)}{(x-5)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-5)(x+1)}({x}^{2}-x+1)}{\\cancel{(x-5)(x+1)}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-1,$ and $x=5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/assets/bca412e444ba3f3126cc88394ea466c48c2dcb60916dcf42ffb0abecb2c5ad48.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-107070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3bf15859013a041badc2d3845fd1acf72b0f97b9d8b99f85c723c09cbdf69333"} {"question" "q-107070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-107070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-1"] ["math" "x=-1,5"] ["math" "x=0,5"] ["math" "x=5"] ["text" "No vertical asymptotes"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-107070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No vertical asymptotes"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From **left to right**, the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x-3}-\\frac{1}{x+7}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x-3}-\\frac{1}{x+7} & =\\frac{x+7-(x-3)}{(x-3)(x+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{(x-3)(x+7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n(x-3)(x+7)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-7\\,,\\,x=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=-7$ and $x=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3bf15859013a041badc2d3845fd1acf72b0f97b9d8b99f85c723c09cbdf69333"} {"question" "q-339769" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339769" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339769" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339769" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{10x}{{x}^{2}+5x}$ is\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10x}{{x}^{2}+5x} & =\\frac{10x}{x(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{x+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx+5=0\\,⟹\\,x=-5\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=-5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3bf15859013a041badc2d3845fd1acf72b0f97b9d8b99f85c723c09cbdf69333"} {"question" "q-339963" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339963" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-16}{{x}^{2}+6x+8}$ is\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-16}{{x}^{2}+6x+8} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-{4}^{2}}{(x+2)(x+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-4)(x+4)}{(x+2)(x+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-4)\\cancel{(x+4)}}{(x+2)\\cancel{(x+4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-4}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx+2=0\\,⟹\\,x=-2\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3bf15859013a041badc2d3845fd1acf72b0f97b9d8b99f85c723c09cbdf69333"} {"question" "q-339975" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005797/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bc8e30a2209c176912896afe7a44d5d8d76b02a34c32a5ae820be724c489d1d"} {"question" "q-339975" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capt